hexagon: the tile flash attention for the decode shapes, in spans of KV rows

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus the patches before this one in patches/series.

Files:
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/flash-attn-ops.c  the conversion phase of a span and the loop of the spans
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/flash-attn-ops.h  the bit HTP_FA_OPT_DECODE, the field spans of the kernel
                                                params, the layout of the spans and the plan
                                                hmx_fa2_find_span_size
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp      the decode shapes and their plan
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp-opnode.h          the form in the profile line

The commit of this patch also gives the check of the spans and their layout to the DSP model of the
hexhost harness (tests/fuzz/hexhost/common/dsp_model.cpp), and it adds the kernel lab target
tools/htp-lab/lab/target_fa2.c.

The defect

At 1 to 8 queries of the 4B, the op goes to HTP_FA_KERNEL_HMX with one q block of 32 rows (8 queries
times the GQA factor 4). At 4096 KV rows the plan has Bc 1344 and 4 KV blocks. Each block moves its K
and V rows through the DMA queue of thread 0, then converts them, runs one QK, one softmax on one thread
and one O update. The phone stage sweep measured the op at 1 query (test-backend-ops perf):

    KV rows     Q8_0 K and V    F16 K and V
    512           74 us           79 us
    4096         371 us          368 us
    16384       1120 us         2209 us

At 16384 KV rows the op reads 35.7 MB of Q8_0 rows (32 GB/s) and 67 MB of F16 rows (30 GB/s). The HMX
matmul reads its weights at 59 to 62 GB/s. At 4096 rows the Q8_0 cache is not faster than the F16 cache.

The change

1. The decode shapes (Q rows times the GQA factor 32 or less) go to HTP_FA_KERNEL_HMX2 with the field
   spans set. The plan has one q block. hmx_fa2_find_span_size selects the largest span of KV rows whose
   layout fits the VTCM, and then divides the KV rows into spans of equal size (a multiple of 64). At
   4096 KV rows there is one span of 4096 rows, and at 16384 rows there are 3 spans of 5504 rows.

2. For each span, all threads move and convert the rows of the span: each thread moves its tiles of 32
   rows with its own DMA queue, 64 rows at a time into two buffers, thus the next transfer runs while
   the thread converts. The buffers share their bytes with the S and P tiles, because the conversion of
   a span ends before its QK. Then the HMX runs the QK of the span, the HVX runs the softmax, and the HMX
   runs the O update. The O tiles and m stay in VTCM from one span to the next. Before the next span
   converts into the same tiles, the kernel waits for the jobs of the span. The thread of the op pushes
   the mask of a span to its own DMA queue after the conversion, when the queue is empty.

3. With spans, the next q block does not start early, because each head has one q block.

4. The kernel refuses the spans form when the queries are more than Br (HTP_STATUS_INVAL_PARAMS).

5. The kernel params get the field spans. mask_broadcast and pipeline become uint8_t fields, thus the
   struct keeps its size limit of 128 bytes. HTP_FA_KERNEL_HMX reads the two fields as before.

6. The bit HTP_FA_OPT_DECODE (2) of GGML_HEXAGON_FA_OPT enables the form (the preset value sets it). The
   profile line gives "hmx2-span/BrxBc vtcm N".

The tests in the kernel lab (tools/htp-lab target fa2, v79, the release flags, the functional simulator,
a reference in double, 16 and 4 heads, head size 256, the code of this patch, 0 DMA queue violations;
measured)

    queries x KV rows    K and V   mask                 VTCM     spans of Bc    NMSE
    2 x 700              Q8_0      causal               1 MB     6 of 128       5.6e-7
    4 x 1500             F16       values in [-1, 0]    2 MB     2 of 768       5.2e-7
    3 x 777              Q8_0      none                 1 MB     7 of 128       6.6e-7
    1 x 1000, sinks      Q8_0      causal               1 MB     8 of 128       1.2e-5

Each run has 0 values that are not finite. The smaller VTCM limits give more spans, thus the runs test the
loop of the spans.

The tests on the host

- tests/fuzz/hexhost/run.sh test none --profile release on the tree with this patch and with the check of
  the spans in the DSP model: 0 findings. The graphs mode passes each path of the 2B and the 4B.
- The host unit and flash-attn-ops.c of v73, v75, v79 and v81 compile with the flags of the release build.

The results on the phone (HTP0, the 4B Q8_0, a Q8_0 cache with flash attention; the stage fak2 of
2026-09-25, its variant E runs the decode shapes in spans)

- test-backend-ops test, the decode cases of the 4B (1 query at 512, 4096, 5000 and 16384 KV rows, 4
  queries at 4096, Q8_0 and F16): each passes.
- The time of one FA op (test-backend-ops perf) at 1 query, against HTP_FA_KERNEL_HMX:

      KV rows, cache type    HTP_FA_KERNEL_HMX    this patch    ratio
      4096, Q8_0             368 us               314 us        0.85
      16384, Q8_0            1187 us              1162 us       0.98
      4096, F16              381 us               360 us        0.95
      16384, F16             1326 us              1321 us       1.00

- The decode tokens at the depth 3072 (GGML_HEXAGON_PROFILE=1): 352 us for each FA op before, 299 us with
  this patch.
- llama-bench tg32, the flags of the app, 1 round: +1.2 % at the depth 0, +1.5 % at 4096, +2.7 % at 16384.
  The release rule: the Q8_0 cache over the F16 cache 1.007 at 4096 and 1.021 at 16384.
- llama-perplexity --kl-divergence against the naive oracle, -b 1: mean KLD 0.000558 +- 0.000068, and
  0.000557 +- 0.000089 for HTP_FA_KERNEL_HMX in the same stage. kvkl at 16384 tokens: the decode tail
  0.000461.
The results of the stage fak3 (2026-09-25, the code of this patch):

- test-backend-ops test, the 12 small and 4 large cases of the 4B and of its encoder: each passes.
- The FLASH_ATTN_EXT suite: refer to the table in the header of hexagon-fa/0001. The decode shapes that
  this patch takes: 0 of 128 cases without sinks fail, and 5 of 119 cases with sinks (HEAD: 2 of 119; on
  the kernel of HEAD the count changes from 26 to 30 of 815 from one run to the next).
- The time of one FA op at 1 query, against HTP_FA_KERNEL_HMX: 0.85 at 4096 and 1.05 at 16384 KV rows for
  Q8_0, 0.96 and 1.03 for F16. In fak2 the same shapes gave 0.85, 0.98, 0.95 and 1.00, and the op of
  HEAD changed by 5 % between the two stages.
- llama-perplexity --kl-divergence, -b 1: mean KLD 0.000558 +- 0.000068, the bits of fak2 (the loop of
  the spans of this patch is shorter than the loop that fak2 ran, and it gives the same result). kvkl at
  16384 tokens: the decode tail 0.000468.
- llama-bench tg32, 2 rounds, against HEAD: +0.9 % at the depth 0, -0.2 % at 4096 (the rounds of HEAD
  11.39 and 11.47, of this patch 11.35 and 11.46), +4.1 % at 16384. The release rule (the Q8_0 cache over
  the F16 cache): 1.008 at 4096 (rounds 1.000 and 1.016) and 1.014 at 16384 (rounds 1.032 and 0.996).

